{
  "headline": "FDA's records show the product is supplied by Strides Pharma Science Limited (FEI 3004554612) whose most recent inspection ended 2026-05-20 and was classified VAI, and a different manufacturer (Salix Pharmaceuticals) has a shortage listing marked To Be Discontinued as of 2026-08-13",
  "headline_cites": ["E11", "E10", "E12"],
  "sentences": [
    {
      "text": "The NDC 64380076721 used at Corvale General, Corvale Lakeside, and Corvale East is labeled by Strides Pharma Science Limited with FEI 3004554612.",
      "cites": ["E2", "E3", "E1", "E11"]
    },
    {
      "text": "FDA inspection 1319788 of that facility ended on 2026-05-20 and received a VAI classification, with the classification known to FDA on 2026-08-14.",
      "cites": ["E10"]
    },
    {
      "text": "A separate FDA shortage listing for the same generic combination under Salix Pharmaceuticals shows a status of To Be Discontinued with an initial posting date of 2026-08-13 and notes a business decision to discontinue manufacture.",
      "cites": ["E12"]
    },
    {
      "text": "Current inventory shows Corvale General holds 272 units at 9.8 per day (28 days on hand), Corvale Lakeside holds 15 units at 1.7 per day (9 days on hand), and Corvale East holds 182 units at 7.3 per day (25 days on hand).",
      "cites": ["D2", "D3", "D1"]
    },
    {
      "text": "Because the links between the Strides-supplied NDC and the Salix discontinuation are weak and the Strides plant's latest inspection is VAI, the root cause for this specific NDC's shortage should be verified with the supplier and FDA.",
      "cites": ["E11", "E10", "E12"]
    },
    {
      "text": "The recommended transfer is to move 9 units from Corvale General to Corvale Lakeside, which would leave Corvale General with about two weeks of supply and bring Corvale Lakeside to approximately 14 days on hand.",
      "cites": ["D2", "D3"]
    }
  ]
}
